# Purpose
# Run output checks, smoke checks, browser checks, and visual artifact checks.
#
# Common usage
# Run from the repository root.
# .\scripts\verify-pages.ps1
# .\scripts\verify-pages.ps1 -Port 4000 -KeepServer
# .\scripts\verify-pages.ps1 -SkipBuild -Port 4000
# .\scripts\verify-pages.ps1 -Browser Chrome -OutputDirectory verification-artifacts\manual-full
# .\scripts\verify-pages.ps1 -KeepServer -DisplayViewports "3440x1440@1","1920x1080@2"
# .\scripts\verify-pages.ps1 -UpdateVisualBaselines
#
# Useful options
# -BaseUri chooses the local site URL.
# -Port chooses the localhost port.
# -BindAddress chooses the local bind address.
# -Browser chooses Auto, Chrome, Edge, or Chromium.
# -OutputDirectory chooses where reports and screenshots are written.
# -DisplayViewports forwards wide and high-DPI cases to verify-browser-pages.ps1.
# -SkipBuild uses the current _site folder.
# -SkipBrowser skips browser verification.
# -SkipScreenshots skips screenshot capture.
# -SkipVisualValidation skips screenshot validation.
# -VisualBaselineDirectory chooses a baseline folder.
# -UpdateVisualBaselines refreshes visual baselines.
# -RequireVisualBaselines fails when a baseline is missing.
# -KeepServer leaves localhost running after checks.
#
# Recommended next command
# Open http://127.0.0.1:4000 in the browser when -KeepServer is used.
#
# Notes
# This is the preferred full verification command.
# It verifies server freshness before browser checks.
# Display profiles use WIDTHxHEIGHT@DPR syntax, including 3440x1440@1 for ultrawide WQHD.
